        "text": "{\"recorded_count\": 18, \"total_count\": 18, \"missing_ids\": [], \"complete\": true, \"results\": [{\"item_id\": \"FT-1\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Searching \\\"data\\\" filtered the job list down to only \\\"Data Scientist\\\" card, matching by title and keyword.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-2\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking the \\\"Data Scientist\\\" card navigated to a details page showing the model graph, coverage, critical path, risk gaps, scenario simulation and template library sections.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-3\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dragging the \\\"Business Acumen\\\" node card to a new canvas location moved it (translate changed from 300,0 to -310.6,-370.3) with the \\\"dragging\\\" class cleared afterward, and all 5 edges (including \\\"Edge from business-acumen to storytelling\\\") remained intact, confirming the model structure is preserved after repositioning.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-4\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No UI mechanism to modify edge weight\", \"actual\": \"Edges display a weight percentage label (e.g. \\\"Edge from python to ml\\\" 90%) but clicking/double-clicking the edge only toggles a \\\"selected\\\" CSS class with no editor, slider, or dialog appearing (dialog count and slider count unchanged before/after). Real mouse clicks on the edge/label are also blocked because overlapping node cards intercept pointer events, making the edge unreachable via normal UI interaction. Only per-node \\\"Weight\\\" sliders exist, which modify the node's own weight, not edge weights.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Node enable/disable switch does not toggle\", \"actual\": \"Clicking the switch control on any competency node (tested Data Visualization and Business Acumen, via real UI click and via programmatic .click()) leaves aria-checked=\\\"true\\\" and node opacity=1 unchanged. No node ever becomes visually grayed out/hidden or excluded, so disabling cannot be verified to affect calculations.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Template Library section lists 5 job templates (Software Engineer, Product Manager, HR Manager, Data Scientist, Sales Manager) each showing category, competency/connection counts, and keyword tags, allowing users to browse and preview template contents before applying.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Applying a template does not actually load its competency graph\", \"actual\": \"Clicking \\\"Apply\\\" on the \\\"Software Engineer\\\" template updated the page header to \\\"Software Engineer\\\"/\\\"Engineering\\\" and changed the Coverage/Avg Level/Critical Path summary text (critical path list showed \\\"Programming Languages, Problem Solving, System Design\\\" - Software Engineer competency names), but the actual rendered graph nodes remained unchanged, still showing the original Data Scientist competencies (Machine Learning, Statistical Analysis, Python Programming, Data Visualization, Business Acumen, Data Storytelling) with their original ids (ml, statistics, python, data-viz, business-acumen, storytelling). The model was not truly loaded into the editing interface.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No naming/description capture and no retrievable 'My Templates' location\", \"actual\": \"Clicking 'Save Current' immediately showed a toast ('Template Saved' / 'Current model configuration has been saved as a template.') with no dialog to name the template or add a description first. After saving, the Template Library list still showed only the same original 5 templates (Software Engineer marked 'Current', Product Manager, HR Manager, Data Scientist, Sales Manager) - no new custom template entry appeared, and no 'My Templates' section exists anywhere on the page to retrieve it.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking Training tab (e529) switched selected state and rendered a distinct tabpanel with heading 'Training Simulation', description 'Model the impact of training programs', and different default Category Adjustment values (technical Level Change +1, domain Level Change +1) vs Recruitment's all-zero defaults. Clicking Promotion tab (e534) similarly rendered heading 'Promotion Simulation', description 'Assess readiness for role advancement', with its own distinct defaults (technical Weight Change -5%, behavioral Weight Change +10%). All three tabs (Recruitment/Training/Promotion) are switchable and show scenario-specific content.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"On the Promotion tab (default adjustments: technical Weight Change -5%, behavioral Weight Change +10%), clicking 'Run Simulation' produced a toast 'Simulation Applied - Competency levels and weights have been adjusted based on the scenario.' The Critical Path indicator changed from 3 competencies (Programming Languages/Problem Solving/System Design) to 4 competencies (Problem Solving/Programming Languages/Collaboration '+1'), demonstrating a quantitative/qualitative change to key indicators as a result of the simulated scenario.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Edited state / explicit save does not persist across navigation\", \"actual\": \"On the Software Engineer model, raised Code Review's level to Expert (5th star), which correctly updated Coverage 68%→74% and Avg Level 3.3→3.7 (Advanced). Clicked the 'Save' button in the header (no dialog/confirmation appeared other than a toast). Then navigated back to the Models list via the back arrow and re-opened Software Engineer. The model reloaded with Coverage back to 68%, Avg Level back to 3.3 (Intermediate), and Code Review's level back to 'Intermediate' - the edit was lost. There is no working persistence mechanism: neither implicit state restoration nor the explicit 'Save' button retains user edits when leaving and returning to a model.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Cannot verify constraint enforcement; underlying edit operations are non-functional\", \"actual\": \"Node disable (switch) does not work (see FT-5), so a \\\"disabled capability\\\" state can never be reached to test edge-to-disabled-node prevention. Additionally, attempting to create new edges via handle-to-handle drag (both a self-loop on Machine Learning and a normal new connection from Data Visualization to Statistical Analysis) produced no new edge and no warning/error message - edge creation appears unimplemented, so there is no observable validation/prevention mechanism for invalid dependency edges.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Raising Machine Learning's level from Advanced to Expert (5th star) immediately updated Coverage from 71% to 75% and Avg Level from 3.5 to 3.7 without needing a page reload.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Node repositioning via drag-and-drop and level-star clicks (which do work) updated the canvas and metrics (Coverage/Avg Level/Risk Gaps) immediately with no observable lag on this 6-node/5-edge graph, which is a moderate complexity model.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Details page shows a React Flow graph with 6 competency nodes (Machine Learning, Statistical Analysis, Python Programming, Data Visualization, Business Acumen, Data Storytelling) and directed weighted edges labeled with percentages (e.g. \\\"Edge from python to ml\\\" 90%, \\\"Edge from statistics to ml\\\" 85%), each node showing level, weight slider, category badge, and enable/disable switch.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Critical path does not recalculate after structural/level changes\", \"actual\": \"The Critical Path metric consistently listed the same 3 competencies (Machine Learning, Python Programming, Statistical Analysis) with count \\\"3\\\" before and after multiple level changes (raising Machine Learning to Expert, lowering Python Programming to Beginner) that did successfully change Coverage/Avg Level/Risk Gaps. Edge-weight editing and node disabling (the other structural levers) are non-functional (see FT-4/FT-5), so no structural change could be applied at all to verify real-time critical-path recalculation; the value observed never changed, suggesting it is a static/precomputed list rather than dynamically recalculated.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Lowering Python Programming's level from Advanced to Beginner immediately updated the \\\"Risk Gaps\\\" metric from \\\"0 identified\\\" to \\\"1 identified\\\" and listed \\\"Python Programming\\\" as a flagged risk gap badge.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"The Risk Gaps metric card (prominently placed in the top metrics strip) shows a circle-alert warning icon next to the heading, and the flagged competency \\\"Python Programming\\\" is rendered as a red destructive-styled badge (bg-destructive/text-destructive-foreground), providing a clear, immediate visual alert.\"}]}"
